# PROJECT IDEA INTAKE

## When this applies

Run this protocol when **any** of the following is true:

1. **Explicit:** The user message **starts with** `PROJECT IDEA INTAKE` or `[NEW PROJECT IDEA]` (case-insensitive for the first line).
2. **Explicit scope line:** Optional second line: `SCOPE: new-standalone-project` | `pool-candidate` | `current-project-feature` | `unknown`.
3. **Chat dump:** The message reads like a **new game / app / product concept** or **big directional idea** — not a concrete coding task (e.g. not “change `foo.ts` line 20” or “fix the crash”). Signals include: new project name, “what if we built…”, standalone game/app, future flagship, compare to existing pool titles.

**Do not** treat as intake: routine bug reports, refactors, “how does X work,” or session scheduling — unless the user asks to file the message as an idea.

If unsure whether it is idea-shaped, ask **one** short question: “Should I run idea intake on this, or were you only thinking out loud?”

## When the user already gave explicit intake

If the message starts with `PROJECT IDEA INTAKE` or `[NEW PROJECT IDEA]` and classification is clear, you may **skip** a redundant “where should this go?” step and instead **state** where you will file it and **ask only if** pool vs notebook is ambiguous.

## Pipeline (order)

1. **Restate** — One plain sentence mirroring the idea (confirm understanding).
2. **Classify** — Pick one primary bucket:
   - **Notebook only** — vague, emotional, “someday,” not ready for pool.
   - **Current product (this repo)** — Feature or addition for the active app; apply the project's scope-creep guard rule if one exists. If out of current phase → `PROJECT_CONTEXT.md` Future Features (or say scope guard line).
   - **Pool candidate** — New standalone project for [docs/FUTURE_PROJECTS_POOL_MASTERLIST.md](docs/FUTURE_PROJECTS_POOL_MASTERLIST.md) — use the **Intake Section** bullet format in that file.
   - **Needs Plan mode session** — Large or cross-cutting → row in [docs/PLAN_MODE_AND_BACKLOG.md](docs/PLAN_MODE_AND_BACKLOG.md) instead of building in chat.

3. **Propose before write (default)** — Say exactly which file(s) you would edit and what you would add (one line / one row). **Do not edit files** until Ryan confirms or adjusts — except when explicit `PROJECT IDEA INTAKE` + obvious single destination was already agreed in the same turn.

4. **Execute after OK** — Touch the **minimum** files. Do not duplicate the same idea in five places.

5. **Pool / canon** — For pool candidates, name **one** primary doc path for a future canon file (e.g. `docs/…` or subproject `CLAUDE.md`). Do not create a full scaffold unless Ryan asks.

6. **Read-back** — Short: what was filed and where. For pool rows, include: **“Adding to the pool does not authorize starting build work.”**

7. **Session log** — If the intake changed durable docs in a substantive way, add a bullet to [PATCH_NOTES.md](PATCH_NOTES.md) in the same session when other exit logging happens (or when Ryan wraps up).

## File map (example — adapt filenames per repo)

- [docs/IDEAS_NOTEBOOK.md](docs/IDEAS_NOTEBOOK.md) — dated one-line / short entries
- [docs/FUTURE_PROJECTS_POOL_MASTERLIST.md](docs/FUTURE_PROJECTS_POOL_MASTERLIST.md) — pool table + intake format
- [docs/POST_PRIMARY_PROJECT_LOCK.md](docs/POST_PRIMARY_PROJECT_LOCK.md) — locked order (reference)
- [docs/PROJECT_PRIORITY_AUDIT.md](docs/PROJECT_PRIORITY_AUDIT.md) — comparison rubric at planning time
- [PROJECT_CONTEXT.md](PROJECT_CONTEXT.md) — Future Features for current-app backlog
- [docs/PLAN_MODE_AND_BACKLOG.md](docs/PLAN_MODE_AND_BACKLOG.md) — queued Plan mode topics

## Optional batch

If Ryan says **“process my idea notebook”** or attaches `docs/IDEAS_NOTEBOOK.md` for intake, run the same pipeline for **each** new unchecked block since last filing (or each new dated entry) — still **propose then confirm** if any row would hit pool or PROJECT_CONTEXT.

